the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    Antrag holds for *a case*.
    Antrag_a holds for *a case*.
    Antrag_b holds for *a case*.
    Nur einmal referenziert holds for *a case*.
    Einfach referenziert holds for *a case*.
    the answer to Nur einmal referenziert for *a case* is *a truth value*; scenario element.
    Nur einmal referenziert would hold for *a case*; unknown.
    the answer to Einfach referenziert for *a case* is *a truth value*; scenario element.
    Einfach referenziert would hold for *a case*; unknown.

the knowledge base r6_2_accept_modular_with_single_parent includes:

the text of the_rulemap is at "sources/accept-modular-with-single-parent.ruml".

Antrag holds for a case if
    Antrag_a holds for the case
    and Antrag_b holds for the case.

Antrag_a holds for a case if
    Nur einmal referenziert holds for the case.

Antrag_b holds for a case if
    Einfach referenziert holds for the case.

Nur einmal referenziert holds for a case if
    the answer to Nur einmal referenziert for the case is true.

% Until a person answers, RUML's answer is undefined: the leaf holds only on the assumption below.
Nur einmal referenziert holds for a case if
    it is not the case that the answer to Nur einmal referenziert for the case is a truth value
    and Nur einmal referenziert would hold for the case.

Einfach referenziert holds for a case if
    the answer to Einfach referenziert for the case is true.

% Until a person answers, RUML's answer is undefined: the leaf holds only on the assumption below.
Einfach referenziert holds for a case if
    it is not the case that the answer to Einfach referenziert for the case is a truth value
    and Einfach referenziert would hold for the case.

